  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The developed models are qualitative rather than quantitative, meaning they map the structure of system feedbacks without simulating numerical trajectories or specific local parameters.",
      "what": "This study develops qualitative system dynamics models and causal loop diagrams to analyze the systemic impacts of shared micromobility, carsharing, ridesharing, and on-demand ride services on urban transportation. By synthesizing variables and causal relationships across multiple existing studies, the models map the non-linear interdependencies and feedback loops that characterize urban mobility systems.",
      "why": "It provides a holistic framework that visualizes the indirect, long-term consequences of shared mobility policies, demonstrating how interventions favoring a single transit mode can unintentionally undermine overall urban sustainability."
